                <h2><a href=3D"https://stochasticfractals.wordpress.com/200=
9/05/04/maximum-of-wiener-brownian-motion/">Maximum of Wiener Brownian&nbsp=
;Motion</a></h2>

                <p style=3D"text-align:left;">Let <img src=3D"https://s0.wp=
.com/latex.php?latex=3DW_0&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=
=3D20201002" alt=3D"W_0" class=3D"latex" width=3D"23" height=3D"16"> be the=
 standard Wiener Brownian Motion process, and <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com=
/latex.php?latex=3DM%28t%29&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=
=3D20201002" alt=3D"M(t)" class=3D"latex" width=3D"38" height=3D"19"> defin=
ed as <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3DM%28t%29%3D%5Cmax_%7B=
0+%5Cleq+s+%5Cleq+t%7D+W_%7B0%7D%28t%29&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp=
;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"M(t)=3D\max_{0 \leq s \leq t} W_{0}(t)" cla=
ss=3D"latex" width=3D"184" height=3D"19">, we then have the following resul=
t:</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3DP%28M%28t%29+%5Cgeq+x%29=
%3D+2%281-%5Cphi%28%5Cfrac%7Bx%7D%7B%5Csqrt%7Bt%7D%7D%29%29&amp;bg=3De6e6e6=
&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"P(M(t) \geq x)=3D 2(1-\=
phi(\frac{x}{\sqrt{t}}))" class=3D"latex" width=3D"227" height=3D"24"></p>
<p>where <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3D%5Cphi&amp;bg=3De6=
e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"\phi" class=3D"late=
x" width=3D"10" height=3D"17"> denotes the standard normal cumulative distr=
ibution function:</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3D%5Cphi%28z%29%3D%5Cfrac%=
7B1%7D%7B%5Csqrt%7B2%5Cpi%7D%7De%5E%7B-z%5E%7B2%7D%2F2%7D&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&a=
mp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"\phi(z)=3D\frac{1}{\sqrt{=
2\pi}}e^{-z^{2}/2}" class=3D"latex" width=3D"132" height=3D"27">    <img sr=
c=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3D%5Cforall%7Bz%7D%5Cin%5Cmathbb%7BR=
%7D&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"\for=
all{z}\in\mathbb{R}" class=3D"latex" width=3D"56" height=3D"14"> </p>
<p>This result is simply a direct application of Theorem 2 from <a href=3D"=
http://www.stat.purdue.edu/research/technical_reports/pdfs/1988/tr88-40.pdf=
">this paper</a> with <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3D%5Cal=
pha%3D0&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"=
\alpha=3D0" class=3D"latex" width=3D"44" height=3D"13"></p>
			=09
